  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday through next Monday)\nIssued at 1142 PM CST Mon Nov 23 2026\n\nOverall a quiet forecast for the extended.  On Thursday we'll be a \nbit on the cooler side as a weak backdoor cold front associated with \nan upper trough over the midwest will linger for just a bit. The \nfront will be pretty weak, and highs are only expected to be a few \ndegrees cooler than Wednesday.  Friday through the weekend will be \npretty mild as the ridge dominates the western CONUS and over the \nSouthern High Plains.  Highs in the 60s for the most part.  Current \nforecast does have a cool down on Sunday, but there is a wide \ndiscrepancy in the models as to if this would still occur, or if the \nwarmer temperatures hold.  That also leave a significant \nquestion mark on Monday as the models diverge from each other.  But \none of the models does hint at a potential strong jet that could \nlead to a breezy to windy day.  \n\nWeber",
